{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PyzTx5HVTQ5eksAXrq3Tm3","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/progress.txt has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65e1815d-40a4-4def-9b3d-354e1ab2bece","uuid":"33c5861a-fd47-465c-9fd9-6c18b0e934ae","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/progress.txt","oldString":"=== Session 2026-03-19T22:35:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 12 - EmployeeMapper integration tests","newString":"=== Session 2026-03-19T22:35:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 12 - EmployeeMapper integration tests\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:45:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 13 - EmployeeValidator unit tests\nChanges: Created EmployeeValidatorTest.java with 5 Mockito-based unit tests covering all 5 acceptance criteria: validateCreate with unique email (no throw), validateCreate with duplicate email (throws DuplicateEmailException), validateUpdate with own email same id (no throw), validateUpdate with another employee's email (throws), validateUpdate with entirely new email (no throw).\nWhy: Pure unit test using MockitoJUnitRunner — no Spring context needed. Mockito mock of EmployeeMapper injected directly via constructor. @Test(expected=...) used for exception assertions (JUnit 4 style). verify() confirms findByEmail is called in success paths.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: S as planned.","originalFile":"=== Harness initialized: 2026-03-19T21:39:25+09:00 ===\nProject type: java-maven\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T21:54:16+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 1 - Employee model class\nChanges: Created Employee.java in com.example.legacy.model with all 8 fields (id, name, email, department, salary, hireDate, createdAt, updatedAt). Added @JsonFormat annotations for date serialization: hireDate as \"yyyy-MM-dd\", createdAt/updatedAt as \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss\". Also fixed pom.xml jackson.version from 2.9.11.1 (nonexistent) to 2.9.10.8. Created EmployeeSerializationTest.java with 5 unit tests covering Jackson date serialization.\nWhy: @JsonFormat defaults to UTC, but spec requires server timezone; ObjectMapper must call setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) to propagate local TZ to @JsonFormat patterns.\nDiscovered: jackson-databind 2.9.11.1 does not exist in Maven Central — corrected to 2.9.10.8. All subsequent items should use this version.\nDifficulty: S as planned, but timezone subtlety added ~10 min debugging.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:10:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 2 - Request/Response DTOs\nChanges: Created EmployeeRequest.java and ErrorResponse.java in com.example.legacy.dto. EmployeeRequest has 5 fields with validation annotations. ErrorResponse has status/message/timestamp fields plus nested FieldError inner class for validation error details.\nWhy: javax.validation 1.1.0.Final lacks @NotBlank and @Email; used org.hibernate.validator.constraints for those two. Standard javax.validation.constraints used for @NotNull, @Size, @DecimalMin.\nDiscovered: javax.validation 1.1 annotation gap — @NotBlank and @Email require Hibernate Validator's own constraints package in this stack.\nDifficulty: S as planned; 5 min to diagnose annotation package issue.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:00:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 3 - Database schema and test resources\nChanges: Created src/main/resources/schema.sql (PostgreSQL DDL with BIGSERIAL), src/test/resources/schema.sql (H2-compatible DDL with BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT), src/test/resources/application-test.properties (H2 in-memory MODE=PostgreSQL config).\nWhy: Used separate DDL files per profile instead of relying on H2 PostgreSQL mode to support BIGSERIAL — avoids runtime DDL failures and is more explicit. H2 test schema uses DROP TABLE IF EXISTS + CREATE TABLE (no IF NOT EXISTS) to ensure clean state per test run.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Followed plan: BIGINT AUTO_INCREMENT for H2, BIGSERIAL for PostgreSQL, MODE=PostgreSQL in JDBC URL for H2 compatibility.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:03:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 4 - Spring application and database configuration\nChanges: Created AppConfig.java (@Configuration, @ComponentScan, @PropertySource), DatabaseConfig.java (DBCP2 DataSource, SqlSessionFactoryBean with type aliases + mapper locations, DataSourceTransactionManager, static MapperScannerConfigurer), WebConfig.java (@EnableWebMvc, Jackson ObjectMapper with local TZ, CORS), WebInitializer.java (AbstractAnnotationConfigDispatcherServletInitializer), application.properties (PostgreSQL defaults).\nWhy: MapperScannerConfigurer is a BeanDefinitionRegistryPostProcessor that runs before @Value properties are resolved — declared static @Bean to avoid premature injection failures. ObjectMapper configured with setTimeZone(TimeZone.getDefault()) per LEARNINGS.md for correct @JsonFormat behavior.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Static @Bean pattern for MapperScannerConfigurer is the standard mitigation for BDRPP ordering issue.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:06:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 5 - Security configuration\nChanges: Created SecurityConfig.java (@EnableWebSecurity, extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter) with HTTP Basic auth, stateless sessions, CSRF disabled, in-memory users (admin/admin123 ADMIN, user/user123 USER), role-based URL patterns (GET requires USER|ADMIN, POST/PUT/DELETE requires ADMIN), custom AuthenticationEntryPoint (401 JSON) and AccessDeniedHandler (403 JSON). Created SecurityWebApplicationInitializer.java (extends AbstractSecurityWebApplicationInitializer) to register DelegatingFilterProxy. Updated WebInitializer.getRootConfigClasses() to include SecurityConfig.\nWhy: AbstractSecurityWebApplicationInitializer is required for Java-config (no web.xml) to register the springSecurityFilterChain filter. SecurityConfig must be in the root context (not servlet context) so it applies to all requests before dispatch. Custom entry points return JSON ErrorResponse instead of default Spring Security HTML/Basic-challenge responses.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Spring Security 4.2 in-memory auth with plain text passwords works without {noop} prefix (that prefix is Spring Security 5+).\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:15:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 6 - EmployeeMapper interface and MyBatis XML\nChanges: Created EmployeeMapper.java interface in com.example.legacy.mapper with 9 methods (findAll, findById, insert, update, delete, countAll, searchByNameOrDepartment, countBySearch, findByEmail). @Param annotations on all multi-param methods. Created src/main/resources/mappers/EmployeeMapper.xml with resultMap for snake_case→camelCase column mapping and all 9 SQL statements. Search uses <choose> dynamic SQL for OR logic: both params → (name LIKE OR dept LIKE), one param → LIKE on that param only. Case-insensitive via LOWER(). INSERT uses useGeneratedKeys=\"true\" keyProperty=\"id\". UPDATE explicitly sets updated_at=CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.\nWhy: resultMap needed because DB columns are snake_case (hire_date, created_at, updated_at) while Java fields are camelCase and mapUnderscoreToCamelCase is not enabled in config. <choose> for search avoids malformed SQL when one param is null (service enforces at-least-one-non-null invariant). CURRENT_TIMESTAMP used instead of NOW() for H2 compatibility in tests.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:20:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 7 - EmployeeValidator\nChanges: Created com.example.legacy.exception package with DuplicateEmailException, NotFoundException, BadRequestException. Created com.example.legacy.validation.EmployeeValidator (@Component) with validateCreate(email) and validateUpdate(currentId, email) methods. validateCreate throws DuplicateEmailException if email already exists; validateUpdate throws only if email belongs to a different employee (id mismatch).\nWhy: Created all three exception classes now (not just DuplicateEmailException) because NotFoundException and BadRequestException are small, needed by Item 9 (service) and Item 10 (exception handler), and creating them now avoids a separate session for trivial boilerplate. EmployeeValidator takes EmployeeMapper via constructor injection for testability.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:30:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 8 - Test infrastructure\nChanges: Created TestAppConfig.java in src/test/java/com/example/legacy/config/ — standalone H2 config with DataSource (MODE=PostgreSQL), DataSourceInitializer (runs test schema.sql on context load), SqlSessionFactoryBean (same mapper XML path as production), DataSourceTransactionManager, and static MapperScannerConfigurer. Created BaseIntegrationTest.java in src/test/java/com/example/legacy/support/ — abstract base with @RunWith(SpringJUnit4ClassRunner.class), @ContextConfiguration(TestAppConfig.class), @Transactional for automatic per-test transaction rollback.\nWhy: TestAppConfig is self-contained (no @ComponentScan, no property injection) to avoid conflicting with production DatabaseConfig/AppConfig beans. H2 in-memory DB with MODE=PostgreSQL and DROP TABLE IF EXISTS in schema.sql ensures clean state on every context load. @Transactional on BaseIntegrationTest rolls back data changes after each test method without needing explicit cleanup. DataSourceInitializer is the standard Spring 4.x mechanism for running schema scripts against an arbitrary DataSource.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. All existing tests continue to pass.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:19:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 9 - EmployeeService interface and implementation + Item 15 - EmployeeService unit tests\nChanges: Created PageResult<T> generic pagination wrapper in com.example.legacy.model. Created EmployeeService interface and EmployeeServiceImpl (@Service, @Transactional) in com.example.legacy.service with 6 methods: getAllEmployees, getEmployeeById, createEmployee, updateEmployee, deleteEmployee, searchEmployees. Created EmployeeServiceImplTest with 18 test methods using Mockito (zero Spring context needed).\nWhy: After insert, re-fetch via findById to get DB-generated createdAt/updatedAt — avoids stale object with null timestamps. searchEmployees normalizes empty-string params to null so mapper <choose> logic works correctly (blank strings otherwise match the \"both non-null\" branch). PageResult totalPages uses Math.ceil to handle non-even division. Both Item 9 and Item 15 completed together since tests were written alongside implementation per 70% test rule.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Mockito MockitoJUnitRunner triggers deprecation warning on Mockito 1.x @RunWith — expected for this stack, tests pass fine.\nDifficulty: M as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:22:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 10 - GlobalExceptionHandler\nChanges: Created GlobalExceptionHandler.java in com.example.legacy.controller with @ControllerAdvice. Handles MethodArgumentNotValidException→400 (with fieldErrors populated from BindingResult), NotFoundException→404, DuplicateEmailException→409, BadRequestException→400, generic Exception→500. ISO 8601 timestamp via LocalDateTime + DateTimeFormatter. Created GlobalExceptionHandlerTest.java with 6 unit tests using standalone MockMvc + inner TestController that throws each exception type. Validation test POSTs invalid JSON and asserts fieldErrors array is populated with correct field names and messages.\nWhy: Using standaloneSetup (no Spring context) keeps the test fast and isolated. LocalDateTime.now().format(ISO_FORMATTER) is sufficient for this stack (Java 8, no timezone offset required by spec). @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class) is last resort only — more specific handlers take priority due to Spring's exception handler resolution order.\nDiscovered: No new discoveries.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:24:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 11 - Model and DTO unit tests\nChanges: Created EmployeeRequestValidationTest.java (14 tests) covering all validation constraints on EmployeeRequest — valid request passes, blank/null/too-long name, blank/null/invalid email, blank/too-long department, null/negative salary, zero salary (boundary), null hireDate. Created ErrorResponseTest.java (8 tests) covering ErrorResponse constructor/setters, FieldError construction, JSON serialization of status/message/timestamp fields, fieldErrors as array, empty fieldErrors as [], null fieldErrors as JSON null. EmployeeSerializationTest.java (5 tests, from Item 1 session) already covered the Employee model portion.\nWhy: Used Hibernate Validator directly via Validation.buildDefaultValidatorFactory() — no Spring context needed, tests are fast. javax.validation 1.1 + Hibernate Validator 5.x correctly evaluates @NotBlank/@Email (Hibernate) and @NotNull/@Size/@DecimalMin (javax.validation). ObjectMapper with no special config correctly serializes null list as JSON null and empty list as [].\nDiscovered: No new discoveries. Jackson serializes null List<T> as JSON null (not omitted or []) by default — confirmed working as expected for spec.\nDifficulty: S as planned.\n\n=== Session 2026-03-19T22:35:00+09:00 ===\nCompleted: Item 12 - EmployeeMapper integration tests\nChanges: Created EmployeeMapperTest.java (20 tests) covering all 9 mapper methods: insert (generated id), findById (positive/negative), findAll (offset+limit pagination, empty result), update (all fields modified), delete (removes record, non-existent id no-op), countAll (zero, positive), searchByNameOrDepartment (name-only, department-only, both OR, no match, pagination), countBySearch (name-only, department-only, both OR), findByEmail (positive/negative). Also fixed pom.xml maven-surefire-plugin to add --add-opens flags (java.base/java.lang, java.lang.reflect, java.io) required for Spring 4.3.x CGLIB to work on Java 9+.\nWhy: Spring 4.3.x bundles CGLIB 3.2.5/ASM 5.x which calls ClassLoader.defineClass() (protected) via reflection when creating @Configuration proxy subclasses. Java 9+ module system blocks this by default. --add-opens allows the reflection access. Without this, every integration test using @ContextConfiguration with a @Configuration class would fail with ExceptionInInitializerError: null. This is a one-time fix that unblocks all future integration tests (Items 13, 14, 17, 18, 19).\nDiscovered: Spring 4.3.x CGLIB + Java 9+ incompatibility requires --add-opens in surefire argLine. The error manifests as ExceptionInInitializerError with null cause, which makes it hard to diagnose without understanding CGLIB internals.\nDifficulty: M actual vs M planned (20 min diagnosing CGLIB/Java module issue, 10 min writing tests).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":6,"newStart":80,"newLines":13,"lines":[" "," === Session 2026-03-19T22:35:00+09:00 ==="," Completed: Item 12 - EmployeeMapper integration tests","+","+=== Session 2026-03-19T22:45:00+09:00 ===","+Completed: Item 13 - EmployeeValidator unit tests","+Changes: Created EmployeeValidatorTest.java with 5 Mockito-based unit tests covering all 5 acceptance criteria: validateCreate with unique email (no throw), validateCreate with duplicate email (throws DuplicateEmailException), validateUpdate with own email same id (no throw), validateUpdate with another employee's email (throws), validateUpdate with entirely new email (no throw).","+Why: Pure unit test using MockitoJUnitRunner — no Spring context needed. Mockito mock of EmployeeMapper injected directly via constructor. @Test(expected=...) used for exception assertions (JUnit 4 style). verify() confirms findByEmail is called in success paths.","+Discovered: No new discoveries.","+Difficulty: S as planned."," Changes: Created EmployeeMapperTest.java (20 tests) covering all 9 mapper methods: insert (generated id), findById (positive/negative), findAll (offset+limit pagination, empty result), update (all fields modified), delete (removes record, non-existent id no-op), countAll (zero, positive), searchByNameOrDepartment (name-only, department-only, both OR, no match, pagination), countBySearch (name-only, department-only, both OR), findByEmail (positive/negative). Also fixed pom.xml maven-surefire-plugin to add --add-opens flags (java.base/java.lang, java.lang.reflect, java.io) required for Spring 4.3.x CGLIB to work on Java 9+."," Why: Spring 4.3.x bundles CGLIB 3.2.5/ASM 5.x which calls ClassLoader.defineClass() (protected) via reflection when creating @Configuration proxy subclasses. Java 9+ module system blocks this by default. --add-opens allows the reflection access. Without this, every integration test using @ContextConfiguration with a @Configuration class would fail with ExceptionInInitializerError: null. This is a one-time fix that unblocks all future integration tests (Items 13, 14, 17, 18, 19)."," Discovered: Spring 4.3.x CGLIB + Java 9+ incompatibility requires --add-opens in surefire argLine. The error manifests as ExceptionInInitializerError with null cause, which makes it hard to diagnose without understanding CGLIB internals."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
